            <ArticleTitle>Soft-tissue causes of metatarsalgia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>579-95</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A soft-tissue cause should always be considered when evaluating metatarsalgia. The history, examination, and plain radiographs can all suggest an avenue of pursuit, be it a potential dermatologic, connective tissue, vascular, neurologic, muscular, or neoplastic process.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
